VegaDNS
-------

VegaDNS manages tinydns zones, records, group defaults and accounts through a
browser. Roles are user, group administrator and senior administrator. AXFR
import is restricted to senior administrators and operator-approved DNS servers.

This security refactor requires PHP 8.4 or newer (8.x), PDO MySQL, MySQL with
InnoDB/utf8mb4, and HTTPS. Rendering and IPv6 handling use native PHP; the vendored
Smarty and Net_IPv6 libraries have been removed. composer.json declares platform
requirements; there are no third-party PHP packages to install or resolve.

Read INSTALL for a new deployment and UPGRADE before replacing a legacy instance.
docs/security-fixes.md maps the security findings to controls and regression tests.
Do not deploy a source checkout without the webserver access rules in INSTALL.

Tests (PHP needs PDO SQLite for the local test suite):
    php tests/security.php
    python3 tests/http_security.py php
    sh tests/publisher.sh

The optional MySQL test environment uses an EMPTY database named vegadns_test:
    VEGADNS_TEST_DSN='mysql:host=127.0.0.1;dbname=vegadns_test;charset=utf8mb4'
    VEGADNS_TEST_USER and VEGADNS_TEST_PASSWORD supply test-only credentials.
    php tests/security.php

Run security.php in a fresh database each time. Tests never use production
configuration. HTTP tests start a loopback-only disposable test server and exercise
file and database session handlers; deployment TLS and DNS tools need separate
acceptance checks. See deploy/ for representative webserver/runtime configuration.

